<title>SWITZERLAND: Tietmeyer says no gold deal yet, but close.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says no gold deal yet, but close.</headline>
<dateline>INTERLAKEN, Switzerland 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said no formal deal had been struck yet on Bonn's plans to revalue the central bank's official reserves, but the two sides were close to an agreement.</p>
<p>He also told reporters at the International Monetary Conference that the talks would not lead to any additional money being transferred from the Bundesbank to Bonn in 1997, but possibly in 1998.</p>
</text>
